Evidence (Git::Raw 0.90, throwaway install /tmp/mcp-wiki-gitraw, never a dependency):
- Git/History.pm calls methods that do not exist: `Tree->entry` (:65, :115; real: `entry_bypath`), `Git::Raw::Oid->new` (:109), `Index->files` (:215), `Index->get` (:232), `Repository->create_commit` (:226; real: `Git::Raw::Commit->create`).
- The walker returns Commit objects but :61 passes them to `lookup` ("commit is not of type Git::Raw::Commit").
- :231 commits the old HEAD tree instead of the index tree; the parent list at :232 is an index entry; :214 dies on a repo without commits.
- `Blob->content` returns bytes and is compared with character-string heading_paths: non-ASCII headings never match, restore would double-encode.
- Over stdio with `--git`: update + rename left `git log` at the initial commit; `get_section_history` answered -32603 "Internal error"; every write still reported success.
- JSON::MaybeXS is imported at History.pm:8 and used nowhere (the only lib/ use; drop it and its cpanfile line if nothing else needs it; t/05 enforces both directions).

Scope: make `auto_commit` (create/update events), `get_section_commits`, `get_section_content_at_commit` and `restore_section` work against the real API: stage the page, write the index tree, commit with HEAD as parent (none on an unborn branch), update HEAD; walk Commit objects; decode blob content as UTF-8. Update History.pm POD to what is true (drop the never-returned `conflict` result and the ignored `reason` option, and the dead `conflict` branch in Server.pm restore_section). Out of scope (own cards): rename/delete commits, which commits get listed, restore newline handling, commit message wording.

Tests: a new opt-in file with plan-level `skip_all` unless `eval { require Git::Raw }`, against a tempdir repo: create + update produce commits; get_section_history returns them; restore_section brings back old text; a non-ASCII heading works. Suite stays green without Git::Raw; run it with PERL5LIB=/tmp/mcp-wiki-gitraw/lib/perl5 to see it pass.

